 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-014\", \"clauses\": {\"determine\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Look at the calendar page shown. What month of the year is shown on this calendar?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 is a question that asks the learner to determine a month from a calendar, so the task verb is produced directly by its question.\"}, \"day_and_month_of_the_year\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F14\", \"template\": \"Look at the {month_name} {year} {cal_word}. What day of the week is {month_name} {date}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F14 is the only family that prints a month name together with a day-of-month number (date, 1 to 31). Its question asks for the day of the week, so the day-and-month object is addressed through that month and date pairing. The date domain is not tied to the month, which is a fault recorded under failing_families, but it does not remove producibility.\"}, \"calendar\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F13\", \"template\": \"Look at the {cal_word} page shown. What month of the year is shown on this {cal_word}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F13 prints the representation word calendar through cal_word, which takes its value from F01 or F15, and both print the gated word calendar.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F05\", \"F07\", \"F08\", \"F09\", \"F14\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Count to the {month}th month.\", \"Look at the {v} {year} calendar. What day of the week is {v} {target_date}?\", \"The {elapsed_label} is the number of days or weeks that have passed.\", \"The {months_label} go from January (1st) to December (12th).\", \"Look at the {month_name} {year} {cal_word}. What day of the week is {month_name} {date}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F05: the template hard-codes the suffix th after {month}, and month prints every integer from 1 to 12 (printed_runs 1 to 12). The values 1, 2 and 3 therefore produce non-ordinal forms instead of 1st, 2nd and 3rd. F07 and F14: the target_date slot (printed_runs 1 to 31) is not coupled to the month slot (v in F07, month_name in F14). The domains therefore allow dates that do not exist for the chosen month, such as day 31 in the months with 30 days and day 30 or 31 in February of 2025. F08: elapsed_label takes the text of F02, whose gated wording is 'how much time has passed'. The template is 'The {elapsed_label} is...', so the printed hint is ungrammatical. The hint also explains passing time in days or weeks, a concept whose lc-level word elapsed time is NOT_YET_KNOWN. F09: months_label takes the text of F03, 'the 12 months', and the template begins with 'The', so the printed sentence has a doubled article. The same template also prints '12th' in the parenthetical, and the cumulative_vocab ordinals run only from 1st to 10th, so that ordinal is outside this lc's gates. The clause mapping is producible, but the families listed above fail Rule 1.\"}",
